#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""AI chat agents of a workspace container (ADR-0037). Standard library only.

``ai-coding-agent serve`` runs in the background in the user's workspace container and
drives the official CLIs there, for the chat panel of the Web UI — the way the Claude
Code and Codex extensions of VS Code drive them:

* Claude Code: ``claude -p`` with stream-json input and output. Permission prompts come
  back to this host (``--permission-prompts host --permission-prompt-tool stdio``) and
  are answered from the chat: allow, allow for the session, deny.
* Codex: ``codex app-server`` (JSON-RPC over stdio, the protocol of the Codex IDE
  extension): threads, turns, approvals of commands and file changes, ChatGPT sign-in
  with a device code.

Chats outlive the browser: the daemon keeps the agents running, records every chat as
JSON lines in ``~/.ai-coding/chats/<project>/`` and replays it to each client that
connects (``ai-coding-agent connect``: stdio <-> the daemon's Unix socket). Users sign
in to their own accounts in the official CLIs; this program never reads credentials.

Client -> daemon (one JSON object per line): ``hello``, ``new`` {agent, mode},
``open`` {session}, ``send`` {session, text, mode}, ``approve`` {session, id, decision},
``interrupt`` {session}, ``login`` {agent}, ``status``.
Daemon -> client: events ``{"t": ..., "session": ...}`` (see ``Session.emit``).
"""

